\cf4 \cb3 Test data contains user's tv program preferences for the next 12 weeks (weeks 31-42). Private/public test data is split BY USERS (50/50) - not by time. Every user from the solution has strictly 5 preferred TV programs, sorted ASC from the most preferred (#1) - has the largest number of views - to the least preferred (#5) - has the lowest number of views among top 5 TV programs FOR EACH USER\cb1 \
\cb3 How expected solution file (stuff you have to predict) was made\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf4 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 all entries with tv_show_id = 0 were removed from TV program schedule files\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 for each user and each TV show user screen time (time user watched the show divided by total duration of the show) was calculated. Only TV shows with high screen time (>= 0.8) were taken into account.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 for each user high-screen time TV shows frequency was calculated\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 for each user **strictly** 5 most frequent TV shows were selected DESC (#1 is the most frequent, #5 is the least frequent amongst top 5) - order matters!\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 You have to guess 5 (space-separated) tv_show_ids for each user - fill submission.csv\cb1 \
